{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789219510,"nonce":"foCH2wO6U9vATBsAMY9HY8wdCHo=","title":"Dynamic -\u003e String and Dynamic -\u003e Array are not unboxed at a Let or a call, and Std.string(anon) prints null","message":"Probes (all pre-existing at 5723a508):\n\n    var ds:Dynamic = \"abc\"; var s2:String = ds; s2.length     // garbage\n    var da:Dynamic = [1,2,3]; var a2:Array\u003cInt\u003e = da; a2.length // garbage\n    strLen(ds); arrLen(da)                                     // same at a call\n\n`maybe_unbox_value` (mir/helpers/boxing.rs) skips a Ptr register for an\nArray/Interface/Anonymous target and its String arm does not match what\n`haxe_box_haxestring_ptr` produced, so the box pointer flows on as the value.\nThe call boundary now applies the same rule as Let (signatures.rs), so both\nsites agree -- and both are wrong for these two kinds.\n\nAlso: `Std.string(ctx)` for a typed anon local prints `null` (the raw anon is\nhanded to haxe_std_string_ptr, which reads it as a box), and\n`var d:Dynamic = ctx; Reflect.fields(d)` crashes with fault=0x6.","files":null}]}